<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> <span class="c4">Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Assassination Rogues</span></span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit or 2550 Hit Rating and 7.5% Expertise or 2550 Expertise Rating. Keep in mind that some abilities such as racial weapon expertise will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your special (yellow damage) hits will no longer be able to miss Dungeon or Raid bosses. Our Poisons are now also based off the melee hit table, meaning that 7.5% is all that it takes to ensure that our Poisons never miss. Your regular swings (white damage) still have a chance to miss up until the dual wield Hit cap of 26.5%. This is calculated by taking the base miss chance of 3%, adding the dual wield penalty of 19%, and then adding 1.5% per level above you that the enemy is for a total cap of 26.5%.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, bosses will no longer be able to Dodge your attacks. They will however still be able to parry them when attacking from their front. For the vast majority of bosses, you will be positioned behind them, and enemies cannot parry from behind.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> <span class="c4">Gemming for Assassination Rogues</span></span></h2>Gemming is fairly straightforward throughout Mists of Pandara. You look to get as much Agility as possible and tend to make socket bonus choices based if they will give you more Agility or equal Agility with additional secondary stats.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76884/agile-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Agile Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Agile Primal Diamond</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c6">Red Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76692/delicate-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Delicate Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Delicate Primordial Ruby</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c11">Orange Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76670/adept-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Adept Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Adept Vermilion Onyx</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c9">Purple Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76680/glinting-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Glinting Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glinting Imperial Amethyst</span></a></div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> <span class="c4">Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Assassination Rogues</span></span></h2>Every profession is viable in Mists of Pandaria Classic, but there are some general outliers that come ahead due to raw stat difference, utility, or an on-use ability.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Assassination Rogues</h4>Engineering remains the same powerhouse it has always been and continues to be the 1 primary profession you will have to be the most optimal you can be. <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126731/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> is the main reason for this with its Mists of Pandaria version granting us 1920 primary stat for 10 seconds on a 1 minute cooldown. <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=142568/nitro-boosts">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_burningspeed.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a> continues to function the same way offering a big speed boost for 5 seconds and attached to your belt socket. There are no new explosives in Mists of Pandaria, so the profession does take a light hit in that regard.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="tailoring">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_tailoring.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tailoring for Assassination Rogues</h4>Tailoring offers <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=125481/lightweave-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweave Embroidery</span></a> with its new version giving 4000 attack power for 15 seconds on a ~1 minute internal cooldown. If you're able to effectively track the proc and line it up with other cooldowns, this profession should at least be tied for 2nd best.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="blacksmithing">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_blacksmithing.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Blacksmithing for Assassination Rogues</h4>
<a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=164/blacksmithing">
<img alt="Blacksmithing" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_blacksmithing.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blacksmithing</span></a> offers the same raw agility bonus as the other professions. What sets it apart from the other standard 320 Agility professions is the ability to stack a large amount of secondary stats which Assassination may end up favoring due to its high value on Haste.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> <span class="c4">Best Crafted Gear for Assassination Rogues</span></span></h3>Crafted items are a great way to get an early boost to your item level and bolster up your stats. While some do require you to be leveled up in the profession that crafts them, there are several BoE options as well that can be bought and sold.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77534/agile-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Agile Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Agile Retinal Armor</span></a> as per every other expansion, remains the best option that we have prior to raiding. This is crafted with the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=202/engineering">
<img alt="Engineering" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a> profession and can be socket with Tinker's Gear such as <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77542/quick-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Quick Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Quick Tinker's Gear</span></a>, allowing you to pick and choose which secondaries you will benefit from.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85824/greyshadow-gloves">
<img alt="Greyshadow Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_leather_raidrogue_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Greyshadow Gloves</span></a> is our pre-bis glove option coming as a crafted BoE from the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img alt="Leatherworking" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a> profession.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85823/greyshadow-chestguard">
<img alt="Greyshadow Chestguard" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_leather_raiddruid_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Greyshadow Chestguard</span></a> is our pre-bis chest option coming as a crafted BoE from the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img alt="Leatherworking" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a> profession.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85828/murderers-gloves">
<img alt="Murderer's Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_leather_raidmonk_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Murderer's Gloves</span></a> is an excellent glove option that becomes available after the release of the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6125/mogushan-vaults">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Mogu'shan Vaults</span></a> raid in which the pattern drops.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85788/chestguard-of-nemeses">
<img alt="Chestguard of Nemeses" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_leather_raidrogue_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Chestguard of Nemeses</span></a> is an excellent chest option that becomes available after the release of the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6125/mogushan-vaults">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Mogu'shan Vaults</span></a> raid in which the pattern drops.</div></li>
<li>
